#This is a sample file distributed with Galaxy that enables tools
#to use MetaPhlAn reference data.
#
#Tab separated with 5 columns (value, name, dbkey, path, db_version):
# - value:     stable identity of the data, "<db>-<build>-<date>"
# - name:      human readable label, shown in the tool form
# - dbkey:     the MetaPhlAn index name, passed to MetaPhlAn as --index
# - path:      absolute path of the directory containing the index and the
#              marker gene metadata (the --bowtie2db argument)
# - db_version: "legacy" for databases created by MetaPhlAn 3 (below v4), the
#              marker content ("SGB") otherwise. Tools use it to decide which
#              command line options are required; HUMAnN for example passes
#              --mpa3 only for legacy databases.
#
#This table is written by the MetaPhlAn data manager, which installs the SGB
#databases (vJan21 and later).
#
#Migrating from the old (4 column) metaphlan_database table: add a fifth
#column with "legacy" to every row. Note that HUMAnN 3.9 can only use
#databases of its own release (index names containing "vJun23") and legacy
#(pre-v4) ones, so an old row for vJan21/vOct22 stays unusable with HUMAnN.
#
#Example:
#mpa_vJun23_CHOCOPhlAnSGB_202403-30092024	MetaPhlAn clade-specific marker genes (mpa_vJun23_CHOCOPhlAnSGB_202403)	mpa_vJun23_CHOCOPhlAnSGB_202403	/path/to/data/mpa_vJun23_CHOCOPhlAnSGB_202403	SGB
#mpa_v30_CHOCOPhlAn_201901	MetaPhlAn 3 clade-specific marker genes (mpa_v30_CHOCOPhlAn_201901)	mpa_v30_CHOCOPhlAn_201901	/path/to/data/mpa_v30_CHOCOPhlAn_201901	legacy
